had not declared, reported under rule E: the framework's SessionStart hook hit zakcode's 95 s hook timeout at the first
turn, so the first model call came at t+104 s. The production serve.log I hold shows 0 hook timeouts in 3,567 lines,
so this belongs to my sandbox until shown otherwise; it cost at most 95 s of a window the loop then left unused.
Two instrument limits found by the run, both mine to fix before sample 2: each wake-up compacted the session, so
the stored message list has no whole-run tool-call denominator; and the trace dir holds ONE file, because every
served beat builds a fresh loop on the same session id and each writes turn_1.jsonl over the last (the usage list is
append-only and complete, the serve.log is complete, and I read the session twice mid-run).

